<title>RUSSIA: Russia 3-mth T-bill yield falls to 42.17 pct.</title>
<headline>Russia 3-mth T-bill yield falls to 42.17 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on a new tranche of three-month GKO discount Treasury bills fell to 42.17 percent at an auction on Wednesday from 54.69 percent at the last auction of three-month paper on October 2, the central bank said.</p>
<p>				    Oct 16	     Oct 2</p>
<p>    Series number	     21071		21070</p>
<p>    Issue volume		3.00 trln rbls   1.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations	     1.00 million	   1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)	    4.80 trln	  3.71 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)	    1.79 trln	  1.49 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds		    1.61 trln	  1.31 trln</p>
<p>    Average price	    89.83 pct	  87.77 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price  89.53 pct	  87.52 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield	    42.17 pct	  54.69 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield 43.56 pct	  55.97 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor (remaining)	98 days	    93 days</p>
<p>    Issue date		 Oct 16, 1996     Oct 2, 1996</p>
<p>    Maturity date	    Jan 22, 1997     Jan 3, 1997</p>
<p>On October 16 the finance ministry is offering 7.50 trillion roubles in an issue of six-month T-bills (series 22054).</p>
<p>It is also repaying about six trillion roubles in maturing six-month T-bill (series 22029) and paying about 621.35 billion roubles in a coupon payment on a two-year interest-bearing OFZ bond maturing in July 98.</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
